WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:05.400
Module 08 · Course 3 · Prove & Show · For entrepreneurs
Marketing & Communications

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.800
Reach the people your idea needs from the start with honest messages, through channels you can sustain.

3
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:31.356
This module helps you plan how to reach the people your idea needs: priority audiences, clear and honest messages, ethical stories, channels you can sustain, a launch campaign and measures of what helps. It answers: who must hear from us, and why?

4
00:00:31.756 --> 00:00:32.356
Why plan before you launch

5
00:00:32.356 --> 00:00:38.400
1. When nobody knows you yet, every message has to earn attention honestly.

6
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:44.074
2. A few well-chosen channels save scarce time for the work itself.

7
00:00:44.074 --> 00:00:51.119
3. With little reputation to fall back on, one problem can define you.

8
00:00:51.519 --> 00:01:03.019
What you will work through: 8.1 Communications strategy · 8.2 Audiences and segmentation · 8.3 Messaging framework · 8.4 Storytelling and ethical storytelling · 8.5 Website, SEO and discoverability · 8.6 Social media · 8.7 Email, newsletters and supporter journeys · 8.8 Content strategy and editorial calendar · 8.9 Campaigns and calls to action · 8.10 Community building and engagement · 8.11 Media relations and press materials · 8.12 Reputation, crisis communication and social media policy · 8.13 Measuring communications performance · 8.14 Recap: Marketing & Communications

9
00:01:03.419 --> 00:01:04.019
What you will have

10
00:01:04.019 --> 00:01:09.322
1. Priority audiences, a core message and supporting messages with proof.

11
00:01:09.322 --> 00:01:15.367
2. A small set of channels, a content calendar and a launch campaign.

12
00:01:15.367 --> 00:01:21.670
3. Simple measures of action, plus crisis essentials ready before launch.

13
00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:22.670
Practical tips

14
00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:29.085
1. Pick one social channel where your audiences already are, and do it well.

15
00:01:29.085 --> 00:01:35.870
2. Start an email list now; people who asked to hear from you matter most.

16
00:01:35.870 --> 00:01:42.915
3. See how our example bakery plans the launch of its market stall.

17
00:01:43.515 --> 00:01:45.515
You create: Your communications plan: audiences, messages, channels, calendar, safeguards and measures.

18
00:01:45.515 --> 00:01:50.315
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

19
00:01:51.815 --> 00:01:54.915
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
